---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Prose from '../components/Prose.astro';

const updated = '8 November 2026';
---

<Base
  title="Privacy Policy — OmniShelf"
  description="How omnishelf.cc and the OmniShelf Android app handle data: cookies, third-party advertising such as Google AdSense, personalised ads and how to opt out, and why the app itself collects nothing."
>
  <div class="shell">
    <Prose>
      <p class="meta">Privacy Policy · last updated {updated}</p>
      <h1>Privacy</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        There are two things called OmniShelf and they behave differently. The
        application on your phone collects nothing. This website, like most websites,
        uses cookies, and may in future show advertising through third-party networks.
        This page describes both, plainly.
      </p>

      <h2>1. The Android application</h2>
      <p>
        The OmniShelf app has no account system, no analytics, no advertising SDK and no
        crash-reporting SDK. Your library, reading progress, bookmarks and notes are
        stored in local storage on your device. Uninstalling the app removes them.
      </p>
      <p>
        The app uses the internet permission only for actions you start: opening an OPDS
        catalogue you added, downloading a book, or fetching a cover. Those requests go
        from your device directly to the server you chose; no server operated by this
        project is involved, and there is none to send anything to.
      </p>
      <p>
        The app requests broad file access so that it can index book files that already
        exist on your device. It reads ebook and document formats and writes only to the
        book folder you choose and to its own directory.
      </p>

      <h2>2. This website: cookies</h2>
      <p>
        omnishelf.cc is a static site. It does not ask you to register, and it does not
        store personal information on a server we run.
      </p>
      <p>
        Cookies may be set by this site or by third parties whose services are embedded
        in it. Cookies are small text files placed on your device that allow a site or a
        service to recognise a browser across visits. We use them, where they appear, for
        two purposes: keeping the site working correctly, and — if advertising is
        enabled — allowing third-party advertising systems to deliver and measure ads.
      </p>

      <h2>3. Third-party advertising, including Google AdSense</h2>
      <p>
        This site may use third-party advertising services, including Google AdSense, to
        display advertising. Third-party vendors, including Google, use cookies to serve
        ads based on a user's prior visits to this website or to other websites.
      </p>
      <p>
        Google's use of advertising cookies enables it and its partners to serve ads to
        you based on your visit to this site and/or other sites on the Internet. This is
        commonly described as personalised or interest-based advertising.
      </p>
      <p>
        These third-party systems operate under their own privacy policies. We do not
        receive, and cannot read, the individual data those systems hold about you. We
        see aggregate reports: how many pages were viewed, roughly which countries
        visitors came from, and whether an ad slot performed. Nothing in those reports
        identifies a person.
      </p>

      <h2>4. How to opt out of personalised advertising</h2>
      <p>You can opt out of personalised advertising in several ways:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          Google Ads Settings —
          <a href="https://adssettings.google.com" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank"
            >adssettings.google.com</a
          >, where you can turn off ad personalisation for your Google account.
        </li>
        <li>
          <a href="https://www.aboutads.info/choices/" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank"
            >aboutads.info/choices</a
          >
          and
          <a href="https://www.youronlinechoices.com" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank"
            >youronlinechoices.com</a
          >, which cover many advertising vendors in the United States and Europe.
        </li>
        <li>
          Your browser's own cookie controls. Blocking third-party cookies generally
          prevents personalised advertising from being delivered, though you will still
          see advertising — it will simply be less relevant.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Opting out does not remove advertising. It stops advertising from being tailored
        to your inferred interests.
      </p>

      <h2>5. Analytics and server logs</h2>
      <p>
        This site does not run a first-party analytics product that profiles individual
        visitors. The hosting provider records standard request logs — IP address, user
        agent, requested path, timestamp — for operational and security purposes. Those
        logs are retained for a short period and are not combined with any other data.
      </p>

      <h2>6. Children</h2>
      <p>
        This site is not directed at children under 13 and does not knowingly collect
        personal information from them. The application is rated for general audiences
        and collects no data at all.
      </p>

      <h2>7. Your rights</h2>
      <p>
        Depending on where you live, you may have the right to request access to,
        correction of, or deletion of personal data held about you, and to object to
        processing. Because this site holds no account data, most such requests concern
        data held by advertising vendors, which you must address to them directly using
        the controls in section 4. If you believe this site holds data about you, write to
        the address below and we will answer within 30 days.
      </p>

      <h2>8. Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p>
        If advertising is enabled on this site, or if the app begins to collect anything
        it does not collect today, this page will be updated first and the date at the top
        will change. The current version describes the site as it is: a static
        publication with no advertising code deployed at the time of writing.
      </p>

      <h2>9. Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions about this policy:
        <a href="mailto:hello@omnishelf.cc">hello@omnishelf.cc</a>. The source code of the
        application is public at
        <a href="https://github.com/tt7247129-sys/omnishelf" rel="noopener" target="_blank"
          >github.com/tt7247129-sys/omnishelf</a
        >.
      </p>
    </Prose>
  </div>
</Base>
